n by a race of interdimensional  beings called a nod to the 80s character  as a result she's now unable to be  mutated she's able to sense other  mutants at a distance it can use  telekinesis and splinter trains her to  be a ninja on par with the turtles in  like less than a year I can get behind  the idea of making her special and  allowing her to be a member of the team  as a fighter because you know that's not  new but by the end of this series she  just feels overpowered and the  explanation and introduction of all this  back stories really clumsily thrown into  quick dialogue and maybe three scenes  throughout the show that every character  just accepts it moves on the kraang  water for some kind of plot to take over  the world but after it fails once they  never really go after her again and just  write it off as a goof whoops I think it  would have been better if they committed  more fully to making April a chosen one  instead of  it so early and I especially think they  could have done with just giving her one  combat thing instead of two because  being a ninja and telekinetic that's  overkill man she's basically kenchi with  eyes I have to mention the relationship  of both April's April and Casey in the  2003 show is a really fun background  element that they develop in a realistic  way over the series but it's never  distracting or overwhelming at first she  can't stand the guy and he thinks she's  pretty stuck-up but as they save each  other's lives and get more involved in  crazy [ __ ] they start to see each  other's good sides and at the end of the  series they get married in an episode  that feels really earned for both of  them 2012 April and Casey definitely  flirt but never really date per se  because the show is too interested in  this god-awful love triangle with  Donatello yes Donatello desperately  wants to show April his bo staff  throughout the show and his jealous of  Casey but she never ends up with either  of them and they attempt to resolve the  triangle multiple times  April lets him down gently and he's like  okay yeah I can take a hint then the  next episode after that he's crushing  again it's especially frustrating when  he goes hey sorry I'm being weird and  overbearing all back off now and then  she kisses him on the cheek and  encourages him again  she's kissing him constantly and just  making it worse at the end of the day  this just means I really can't tell what  April wants as a character or where the  writers were intending to go with this  because eventually they just drop it  entirely around the middle of the fourth  season without any conclusion I guess  maybe they didn't have a plan for it and  being wishy-washy about the direction  just led them to giving up on it because  it wasn't getting any  oh geez too much talking about awkwardly  aborted relationship subplots I feel  like we're talking about Star Wars let's  talk about the villains I'm sorry to  have to cut this video and half dear  viewers but I need to get something  uploaded and I need to let you all know  that here at old Godzilla Mendoza  industries we've fallen on some hard  times January in February the lowest  months for views and revenue for any  youtuber and it's become increasingly  clear that using YouTube ads as my main  source of online income is preposterous  so now I'm doing the Burnie meme and  asking for your help I know I don't  advertise my patreon often but I figured  that if just 3% of my subscribers on  YouTube gave me one dollar a month just  one dollar I'd be pretty much set  forever so I'm asking you please be in  that 3% to help me keep the lights on so  I can keep making these videos part two  of this on the way soon  [Music]  [Music]
 

